                "senderName": "NWS Medford OR",
                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 17 at 2:28PM PST until November 18 at 7:00AM PST by NWS Medford OR",
                "description": "* WHAT...Southeast winds 20 to 30 mph with gusts up to 45 mph\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern and central Jackson County, including Ashland,\nPhoenix, Talent, and Medford. This includes portions of Interstate\n5 and highway 140.\n\n* WHEN...From 7 PM this evening to 7 AM PST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result. Winds\nmay damage holiday decorations.",
                "instruction": "Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles. Use extra caution.",
